**C++ Smart Pointers**

C++ smart pointers are a type of object that automatically manage memory for you, eliminating the need for manual memory management with new and delete.

### Types of Smart Pointers in C++

1. **Unique Pointer (std::unique_ptr)**: A unique pointer is a smart pointer that owns and manages another object through a pointer. The pointer is exclusive and cannot be shared with anyone else. When the unique pointer goes out of scope, it automatically deletes the managed object.

   ```cpp
#include <memory>

int main() {
    std::unique_ptr<int> ptr(new int(10));
    // ptr is the owner of the object, it will be deleted when ptr goes out of scope
    return 0;
}
```

